# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# LIQUID MARBLE — a fast 2-D water+oil sim (ling-physics liquid.rs) mapped onto a
# spinning 3-D surface. The two fluids are immiscible: physics decides the
# interface, so the blue water and amber oil only blend where they actually meet.
# The surface cycles plane → sphere → cylinder → cone → dome. Autoplaying.
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

bind start = do {
    open_window(1000, 720)
    set_ambient(0.4)
    set_zdist(7.0)
    bind ui = font_load("assets/fonts/Exo2.ttf", 600.0)
    if ui < 0.0 { bind ui = font_load("../../assets/fonts/Exo2.ttf", 600.0) }

    bind GW = 84.0
    bind liq = liquid_new(GW, GW)
    # seed: a band of water and a band of oil that will slosh and separate
    bind sx = 0.0
    while sx < GW {
        liquid_splat(liq, sx, GW*0.30, 1.0, 0.9, 2.2)    # oil  (kind 1)
        liquid_splat(liq, sx, GW*0.68, 0.0, 1.0, 2.4)    # water (kind 0)
        bind sx = sx + 3.0
    }

    while window_is_open() {
        bind t = time_now()
        # rotate gravity to slosh the fluids around the surface
        liquid_gravity(liq, sin(t*0.6) * 55.0, cos(t*0.6) * 55.0)
        liquid_step(liq, 0.016)
        liquid_step(liq, 0.016)
        # keep topping up so it never drains
        if sin(t*1.3) > 0.9 { liquid_splat(liq, GW*0.5 + sin(t*4.0)*20.0, GW*0.5, 0.0, 0.8, 3.0) }
        if cos(t*1.1) > 0.9 { liquid_splat(liq, GW*0.5 + cos(t*3.0)*20.0, GW*0.4, 1.0, 0.7, 3.0) }

        set_color(6, 7, 14)
        fill()
        set_camera(cos(t*0.3), sin(t*0.3), cos(0.4), sin(0.4))

        # cycle through the surfaces every 6 s
        bind kind = floor(t / 6.0)
        bind kind = kind - floor(kind / 5.0) * 5.0
        liquid_draw_surface(liq, kind, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 2.2, 3.2)

        bind names = ["PLANE", "SPHERE", "CYLINDER", "CONE", "DOME"]
        set_blend(1)
        set_color(0, 230, 255)
        if ui < 0.0 { ui_text(36.0, 22.0, 22.0, "LIQUID MARBLE") } else { font_text_fill(ui, 36.0, 22.0, 26.0, "LIQUID MARBLE") }
        set_color(120, 255, 180)
        if ui < 0.0 { } else { font_text_fill(ui, 36.0, 60.0, 18.0, names[kind]) }
        set_blend(0)
        present()
    }
}
